# Reviewers requested automatically when a pull request opens.
#
# A catch-all, so nothing in the repository can be changed without a review
# being asked for.
#
# Requesting a review is not requiring one: that comes from the `main` ruleset.
# This file decides WHO is asked; the ruleset decides whether the answer is
# needed before merge.
#
# ORDER MATTERS, AND IT IS NOT SPECIFICITY. The last matching pattern wins, so
# the catch-all goes first and path-scoped entries go below it. A catch-all at
# the bottom would override every specific owner above it.
#
# Every repository needs its own copy: CODEOWNERS is not one of the default
# community health files an organisation's `.github` repository provides, so
# ownership does not cross repository boundaries.
